{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781694748,"nonce":"8mFCHWM2xWRqSaVapnK9CiCDDOU=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFxv7pA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/292","origin":"github"},"title":"Enable speed-normalized cross-track gain schedule on BizzyBoat (tune live next deployment)","message":"## Goal\nEnable the new speed-normalized cross-track gain schedule on BizzyBoat by adding the two `FollowPath.pid.*` params to `bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`, then **validate and tune them live on the next deployment**.\n\nThe gain-schedule mechanism merged in [rolker/unh_marine_navigation#76](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/76) (PR #78) but ships **default-off** (`gain_ref_speed: 0.0`) — so it does nothing until a platform opts in. This issue is the opt-in for BizzyBoat.\n\n## Why enable without a prior sim/bench test\nThe params are **live-tunable** via the controller's on-set-parameters callback, so the anchor can be adjusted on the fly during the run:\n```\nros2 param set /bizzy/controller_server FollowPath.pid.gain_ref_speed 1.8\nros2 param set /bizzy/controller_server FollowPath.pid.gain_v_min 0.5\n```\nThe next deployment **is** the test — start from the overlay anchor, sweep speed, and tune live. Instant revert hatch: set `FollowPath.pid.gain_ref_speed 0.0` to disable (falls straight back to the current flat-gain behavior).\n\n## Change\nAdd under the inner-crabbing `FollowPath` block in `nav2_overlay.yaml` (same namespace as `cross_track_error_slew_rate` / `pid.*`):\n```yaml\n      # Speed-normalize the cross-track gain (1/v law) to hold the cross-track\n      # response constant across speed — kills the 3.5 kt limit cycle seen at\n      # Massabesic (rolker/unh_marine_navigation#76). Live-tunable; 0.0 = revert.\n      pid.gain_ref_speed: 1.8   # 3.5 kt anchor (where pid.p:-13 is known-good)\n      pid.gain_v_min: 0.5       # divisor floor; no blow-up at creep / station-keep\n```\n\n## Starting anchor (to be confirmed on the water)\n- `gain_ref_speed: 1.8` m/s — the 3.5 kt point where the field `pid.p: -13` mitigation tracks cleanly.\n- `gain_v_min: 0.5` m/s.\n- **Caveat:** the issue-#76 analysis notes the `−20 → −13` field drop is bigger than a pure `1/v` law predicts (~14% over 3.0→3.5 kt) → extra speed-dependent dynamics (yaw inertia / actuator lag). The `1/v` is the right *shape*; the anchor may want an empirical breakpoint fit from a live speed sweep. Expect to tune.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Overlay carries `pid.gain_ref_speed` / `pid.gain_v_min`.\n- [ ] Next deployment: speed sweep (3.0 / 3.5 / 3.75+ kt) with the schedule on; cross-track RMS roughly constant across the range and no limit cycle.\n- [ ] Final anchor recorded back here (and folded into the overlay if it moved from 1.8).\n\nPart of [rolker/unh_marine_navigation#76](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/76). Field tuning context: rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#289 (2026-06-16 Lake Massabesic).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}